## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design robust, scalable ingestion with strong per-tenant data governance. Probes data quality enforcement, quarantine strategy, schema evolution, and backpressure handling under real-world load.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant data quality validation at ingestion
- Quarantine (bad records) with audit trails
- Schema evolution using Glue catalog and compatible formats
- Backpressure handling via DLQ and adaptive sampling
- Observability: per-tenant quality metrics and alerts

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: per-tenant validation at ingress
function validateAndRoute(event, tenantConfig) {
  const validationResult = validateEvent(event, tenantConfig);

  if (validationResult.isValid) {
    writeToValidStream(event);
    updateMetrics(tenantConfig.tenantId, 'valid');
  } else {
    quarantineRecord(event, validationResult.errors, tenantConfig);
    updateMetrics(tenantConfig.tenantId, 'invalid');
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Privacy and governance in telemetry pipelines are critical; this question probes tenant isolation, data masking, erasure guarantees, and cross-region consistency under cost constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-scoped partitioning and access control
- PII masking at ingest; tombstones for erasure
- Immutable audit trail via OpenTelemetry and S3 Object Lock concepts
- Cross-region replication and DR testing with Glue/Athena catalog
- Cost and latency trade-offs between Lambda and Fargate

## Code Example

```javascript
// PII masking at ingest
function maskPII(record) {
  if (!record.user) return record;
  const masked = { ...record };
  if (masked.user.email) masked.user.email = masked.user.email.replace(/@.*/, "@redacted");
  if (masked.user.phone) masked.user.phone = masked.user.phone.replace(/\d{4,}$/,"****");
  return masked;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test purge latency and ensure tombstones are not resurrected?
- How would you audit cross-region replicas for data residency compliance?
